IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdcsa-types`
IMPORT `cdcsa-common`
IMPORT `cdcsa-scheme`
IMPORT `cdcsa-maternity-adoption`
IMPORT `cdcsa-fathers-shared`
IMPORT `cdcsa-childcare`
IMPORT `cdcsa-general-offences`

-- Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this parent and this child, what paid leave or Government payment
--    does the Act give, how much may be paid, and how much may the employer
--    claim back from the Government?"
--
-- One answer through Part 3: which scheme the child belongs to (Goal 1);
-- the parent's own leave — maternity, adoption or paternity — or, for a
-- self-employed parent, the claim for lost income, or, failing both, the
-- Government-paid benefit (Goals 3-5); and shared parental leave, by
-- arrangement for an April 2025 Scheme child or by the mother's election for
-- an earlier child (Goal 6). Childcare leave (Goal 7), the Scheme (Goal 2) and
-- recovery and offences (Goal 8) answer their own questions.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Parental position` HAS
    `an April 2025 Scheme child`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `a January 2024 Scheme child`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `own paid leave`                             IS A MAYBE `Leave payments`
    `own claim for lost income, at most`         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `Government-paid benefit, at most`           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `shared parental units`                      IS A NUMBER
    `shared parental leave`                      IS A MAYBE `Leave payments`
    `shared parental claim from the Government, at most` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 2, 9, 9A, 10, 12A-12AD, 12DA-12DD, 12E-12J; Second Schedule
GIVEN p IS A `Parent case`
GIVETH A `Parental position`
`the parental position for` p MEANS
    `Parental position` WITH
        `an April 2025 Scheme child`                 IS `april`
        `a January 2024 Scheme child`                IS `jan`
        `own paid leave`                             IS IF `employee` AND `own eligible` THEN JUST `own leave` ELSE NOTHING
        `own claim for lost income, at most`         IS IF `self-employed` AND `own eligible` THEN JUST `own claim` ELSE NOTHING
        `Government-paid benefit, at most`           IS IF (NOT `own eligible`) AND `benefit eligible` THEN JUST `benefit` ELSE NOTHING
        `shared parental units`                      IS `units`
        `shared parental leave`                      IS IF `employee` AND `own eligible` AND `units` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST (`shared parental leave payments for` `units` `units, gross pay per week` `gross`) ELSE NOTHING
        `shared parental claim from the Government, at most` IS
            BRANCH IF `units` EQUALS 0                            THEN NOTHING
                   IF `self-employed` AND `own eligible`           THEN JUST (`the Government pays a self-employed parent at most for` `units` `units, lost income per week` `gross`)
                   IF april AND (NOT `own eligible`) AND `benefit eligible` THEN JUST (`the shared parental benefit at most for` `units` `units, total income per day` (w's `total income per day in the prescribed period`))
                   OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        w MEANS p's `work`
        e MEANS p's `event`
        n MEANS p's `specified event number`
        `april` MEANS `an April 2025 Scheme child` e
        `jan`   MEANS `a January 2024 Scheme child` e
        `employee`      MEANS w's `status` EQUALS `an employee`
        `self-employed` MEANS w's `status` EQUALS `a self-employed person`
        `months` MEANS w's `months of service or of carrying on before the event`
        `gross`  MEANS w's `gross pay (or lost income) per week of work days`
        `daily`  MEANS w's `total income per day in the prescribed period`
        `married` MEANS p's `lawfully married to the other parent in time`
        `mother` MEANS p's `role` EQUALS `the natural mother` OR p's `role` EQUALS `the adoptive mother`
        -- s 12E(7): the mother of an earlier child gives up the weeks she elects
        `given up` MEANS IF mother AND (NOT april) THEN p's `weeks elected by the mother under s 12E(5)` ELSE 0
        -- Own leave or a claim for lost income needs a current employer or
        -- trade; a parent who "is or was" employed but is neither now goes to
        -- the Government-paid benefit (ss 9(5A), 12A, 12HA). Fixed after the
        -- independent pass.
        `own eligible` MEANS (`employee` OR `self-employed`) AND `own eligible on the facts`
        `own eligible on the facts` MEANS
            CONSIDER e
            WHEN `a birth` b THEN
                CONSIDER p's `role`
                WHEN `the natural mother` THEN
                    IF   (NOT b's `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)`) AND `eligible under s 9A(1A), with months of service` months `, for` b
                    THEN REFUSE "the child became a citizen after birth: s 9(1A)-(1B) and (4A) apply; ask `the s 9(1A) outcome under s 76(1)` and `the s 9(1B) options`"
                    ELSE `eligible under s 9A(1), with months of service` months `, for` b
                WHEN `the natural father` THEN `a natural father eligible for paternity leave, birth` b `, married in time:` married `, months of service` months
                OTHERWISE FALSE
            WHEN `an adoption` a THEN
                CONSIDER p's `role`
                WHEN `the adoptive mother` THEN `eligible for adoption leave under s 12AC(1), months of service` months `, adoption` a
                WHEN `the adoptive father` THEN `an adoptive father eligible for paternity leave, adoption` a `, months of service` months
                OTHERWISE FALSE
        `benefit eligible` MEANS
            CONSIDER e
            WHEN `a birth` b THEN
                CONSIDER p's `role`
                WHEN `the natural mother` THEN `eligible for the Government-paid maternity benefit under s 9A(2)` b w
                WHEN `the natural father` THEN `eligible for the Government-paid paternity benefit, event` e `, married in time:` married `, work` w
                OTHERWISE FALSE
            WHEN `an adoption` a THEN
                CONSIDER p's `role`
                WHEN `the adoptive mother` THEN `eligible for the Government-paid adoption benefit under s 12AC(2)` a w
                WHEN `the adoptive father` THEN `eligible for the Government-paid paternity benefit, event` e `, married in time:` married `, work` w
                OTHERWISE FALSE
        `own leave` MEANS
            CONSIDER p's `role`
            WHEN `the natural mother`  THEN `maternity leave payments, specified event` n `, weeks given up under s 12E` `given up` `, gross pay per week` `gross`
            WHEN `the adoptive mother` THEN `adoption leave payments, specified event` n `, weeks given up under s 12E` `given up` `, gross pay per week` `gross`
            OTHERWISE                       `paternity leave payments, an April 2025 Scheme child:` april `, gross pay per week` `gross`
        `own claim` MEANS
            CONSIDER p's `role`
            WHEN `the natural mother`  THEN `the Government pays a self-employed mother at most, specified event` n `, lost income per week` `gross`
            WHEN `the adoptive mother` THEN `the Government pays a self-employed adoptive mother at most, specified event` n `, lost income per week` `gross`
            OTHERWISE                       `the Government pays a self-employed father at most, a January 2024 Scheme child:` jan `, lost income per week` `gross`
        `benefit` MEANS
            CONSIDER p's `role`
            WHEN `the natural mother`  THEN `the Government-paid maternity benefit at most, specified event` n `, total income per day` `daily`
            WHEN `the adoptive mother` THEN `the Government-paid adoption benefit at most, specified event` n `, total income per day` `daily`
            OTHERWISE                       `the Government-paid paternity benefit at most, a January 2024 Scheme child:` jan `, total income per day` `daily`
        -- Shared parental units: an April 2025 Scheme child, by arrangement
        -- (s 12DD; the Second Schedule default if none is given) for a parent
        -- eligible for own leave or a Government-paid benefit (ss 12DA(1),
        -- 12DC(1)); an earlier child, the weeks the mother elected for a father
        -- eligible under s 12F.
        `units` MEANS
            IF april
            THEN IF `own eligible` OR `benefit eligible`
                 THEN CONSIDER p's `units allocated under the arrangement`
                      WHEN JUST u  THEN u
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN `the default units for a parent of` e `, both parents eligible:` (p's `the other parent is also eligible for shared parental leave`)
                 ELSE 0
            ELSE IF `father may take elected leave` THEN p's `weeks elected by the mother under s 12E(5)` ELSE 0
        `father may take elected leave` MEANS
            CONSIDER e
            WHEN `a birth` b THEN
                    p's `role` EQUALS `the natural father`
                AND `a natural father may take elected shared parental leave, birth` b `, married in time:` married
            WHEN `an adoption` a THEN
                    p's `role` EQUALS `the adoptive father`
                AND `an adoptive father may take elected shared parental leave, adoption` a `, married in time:` married
